00:08:39.929 --> 00:08:41.512
- Adopt the mode of

00:08:42.954 --> 00:08:44.287
authentic being.

00:08:45.221 --> 00:08:47.494
And that is something like

00:08:47.494 --> 00:08:49.982
refusing to participate in

00:08:49.982 --> 00:08:52.206
the lie, in deception in the lie.

00:08:52.206 --> 00:08:56.831
To orient your speech as much
as you can towards the truth.

00:08:56.831 --> 00:08:59.307
And to take responsibility
for your own life

00:08:59.307 --> 00:09:01.699
and perhaps also for the
lives of other people.

00:09:01.699 --> 00:09:04.712
And there's something about
that that's meaningful

00:09:04.712 --> 00:09:06.679
and responsible and noble

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:09.617
but also serves to
mitigate the very suffering

00:09:09.617 --> 00:09:12.684
that produces say denialism or the

00:09:12.684 --> 00:09:15.517
flee into the arms of or or the or

00:09:16.401 --> 00:09:20.278
or the escape into the arms of
totalitarians to begin with.

00:09:20.278 --> 00:09:22.449
You need something to shelter you against

00:09:22.449 --> 00:09:23.860
your own vulnerability.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:26.332
- You know you're watching
a movie and you hear a line

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:27.733
and it feels like oh they thought that was

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:29.159
going to be a line in the trailer.

00:09:29.159 --> 00:09:32.058
Like you just know that
on the set someone's like

00:09:32.058 --> 00:09:33.804
that's a trailer mode, like it doesn't

00:09:33.804 --> 00:09:36.957
because it doesn't feel
real necessarily in life

00:09:36.957 --> 00:09:38.611
but it just feels like
ah, it's a great sound

00:09:38.611 --> 00:09:40.004
but it's a great thing.

00:09:40.004 --> 00:09:42.013
That there's a visual equivalent of that.

00:09:42.013 --> 00:09:43.630
And you got to be really
careful because sometimes

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:45.725
I'll think, ah, this is
like one of those moments

00:09:45.725 --> 00:09:47.417
and then you end up
doing it and the truth is

00:09:47.417 --> 00:09:50.762
it ends up feeling posed, it
just doesn't feel authentic.

00:09:50.762 --> 00:09:52.930
I try for those sometimes
they never seem to work.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:55.484
I think that the key for any of this stuff

00:09:55.484 --> 00:09:58.116
and you know whether we've
accomplished it or not

00:09:58.116 --> 00:09:59.005
is up to the audience.

00:09:59.005 --> 00:10:02.099
But I think that the key
to any movie working.

00:10:02.099 --> 00:10:05.838
Certainly a movie called
Star Trek which you know

00:10:05.838 --> 00:10:08.421
could you know be seen as campy

00:10:10.334 --> 00:10:13.139
is finding authenticity.

00:10:13.139 --> 00:10:17.205
And and it's whether
it's in a little nuance,

00:10:17.205 --> 00:10:19.430
a little moment, a character exchange,

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:22.282
a look, a glance, or a huge plot point

00:10:22.282 --> 00:10:24.932
there's something for me that is

00:10:24.932 --> 00:10:26.844
if I don't really
understand what's going on,

00:10:26.844 --> 00:10:29.212
if I can't really get into under the skin

00:10:29.212 --> 00:10:32.126
of these characters, none of the
spectacle is going to matter.

00:10:32.126 --> 00:10:34.134
- And I give it my all I mean I

00:10:34.134 --> 00:10:37.441
I practice every day and I try and stay

00:10:37.441 --> 00:10:39.403
authentic and uncompromising.

00:10:39.403 --> 00:10:43.403
We don't play any you
know crowd-pleasing stuff.

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:46.633
We don't you know get out there and play

00:10:46.633 --> 00:10:48.532
When The Saints Go Marching In.

00:10:48.532 --> 00:10:52.040
And you know will we play
blues, hymns, ragtime,

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.457
whorehouse music.

00:10:54.659 --> 00:10:56.897
Stuff that was authentically New Orleans.

00:10:56.897 --> 00:11:01.382
And we play it in the New
Orleans style as best we can.

00:11:01.382 --> 00:11:05.330
And so I don't feel that I'm a sellout.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.780
I'm doing the best I can.

